  "goodToKnow": "Die Biodiversität is biodiversity; the everyday German word is die Artenvielfalt. A 2017 study based on data from amateur entomologists in Krefeld found that flying insect biomass in German nature reserves had fallen by more than 75 percent in 27 years, sparking debate about das Insektensterben. In 2019 Bavaria's citizens' initiative Rettet die Bienen gathered about 1.7 million signatures. It has no plural."
